@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Coursework loop: real observations before formal analysis
start
:Collect and manually transcribe\n10-15 real Yaounde statements;
:Preserve exact wording and provenance;\nrecord all three members and method;
if (Authentic statements supplied?) then (yes)
  :Explicitly save selected-project Sentence entries;
else (no)
  :Keep evidence incomplete;\nreferences/practice cannot replace fieldwork;
  stop
endif
:Inspect regex tokens, nouns/verbs/slang,\nmultiword phrases, unknowns and code-mixing;
:Interpret frequency and spelling variation;
:Construct or revise CFG from observed structures;\nsave the group's rationale;
:Compute recursion removal / left factoring,\nFIRST/FOLLOW and predictive table;
if (Valid bounded LL(1) grammar?) then (yes)
  :Run table-driven parser over own tokenized inputs;
else (no)
  :Inspect validation errors/conflicts;\nrevise grammar, never choose a rule arbitrarily;
  stop
endif
:Discuss accepted and rejected cases;\nfit is not a judgment of natural speech;
:Capture genuine analyzer screenshots;\nauthor linguistic discussion and limitations;
:Export DRAFT report / slides / artifacts;
if (Human evidence and pagination reviewed?) then (yes)
  :Confirm 25-30 pages, maximum 30;\nrehearse 10 minutes, 3 per member + shared minute;
else (no)
  :Retain DRAFT status and complete missing work;
  stop
endif
:Group reviews submission for 29 September 2026;
stop
legend bottom
  This activity combines implemented software steps and explicitly human coursework tasks.
  Suggested topic coverage is a discussion aid, not a mandatory one-sentence-per-topic gate.
  The default CFG is illustrative until justified against real statements.
  Export is not evidence certification and is separate from the engineering SRS/SDD.
endlegend
@enduml
